    <p>The trustees may fix fees for voluntary membership in the organization established at a state university. Notwithstanding any law to the contrary, if a student body organization is established at any state university, the trustees may fix fees for voluntary membership in that organization, provided that the fees shall not be excessive, and that the trustees shall prescribe, and upon all regular students enrolled in the university, the trustees shall fix a reasonable fee for the use of the facilities of the university, and the trustees shall prescribe the manner in which the fees shall be charged to students. The trustees may approve an increase or decrease in the student body fee only after the fee increase or decrease has been approved by a majority of students voting in a referendum established for that purpose.</p>
